          "content": "```c\n#include <stddef.h>\n\n/* Returns the index of the first occurrence of target in sorted array a,\n   or -1 if target is not present. */\nint first_occurrence(const int *a, size_t n, int target) {\n    size_t lo = 0;\n    size_t hi = n;  /* search range is [lo, hi) */\n\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        size_t mid = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;\n\n        if (a[mid] < target) {\n            lo = mid + 1;\n        } else {\n            hi = mid;\n        }\n    }\n\n    if (lo < n && a[lo] == target) {\n        return (int)lo;\n    }\n    return -1;\n}\n```\n\nThis is a lower-bound style binary search. When duplicates exist, it keeps moving `hi` left when `a[mid] >= target`, so it finds the first occurrence.\n\nFor an empty array, `n == 0`, so `lo == hi == 0`; the loop does not execute, and the function returns `-1`. It does not access the array, so passing `NULL` with `n == 0` is also safe for this function.",
